Kompakt: the notification LED dims a steady light by PWM duty

The level the lights HAL asks for reached the sink current field (patch
0028's log showed levels 1 to 6 arriving), yet a steady light looked the
same at every level. A steady RGB light now runs in PWM mode at 1 kHz and
full current with a duty of level/32, the chip's own dimming in 32 steps;
max_brightness is 32 so the HAL's 0 to 255 maps onto them. A breathing
light (the timed nodes) still sets the peak current, now scaled from the
32 levels to the six current steps. The brightness read back for an RGB
sink is the level it was given. The kernel log line now reads the DIM and
ISINK registers back after each write, so what the chip holds is visible
in logcat (tag kompakt-led).

